---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';

const mail = `mailto:${site.contactEmail}`;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description="How the TossLess app and website handle your data: what stays on your iPhone, barcode lookups, purchases, analytics and the email waitlist."
>
  <div class="wrap page prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="meta">Last updated: 31 October 2026</p>

    <p class="summary">
      <strong>In short:</strong> this page covers two things, the TossLess app and the tosslessapp.com website. The app has no account and keeps
      your food list on your iPhone. The only things that leave your phone are a barcode number when you scan one, and purchase details when you
      buy TossLess Pro. The website counts visits and runs an optional email waitlist. We never sell data.
    </p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    {/* OWNER: the original text named the person who makes the app ("[YOUR NAME]"). The site keeps the owner anonymous, so this says "the TossLess team". Replace it with your name or company if the law or Apple requires an identifiable publisher. */}
    <p>
      TossLess is an iPhone app made by the TossLess team (“we”, “us”). If you have a question about this policy or your data, write to
      <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2 id="app">The TossLess app</h2>
    <p>This part covers the iPhone app.</p>

    <h3>What stays on your iPhone</h3>
    <p>
      Everything you enter in TossLess is stored only on your device. That includes the food you add, its dates, storage place and quantity, your
      shopping list, what you marked as eaten or tossed, and your settings, such as reminder time, appearance and currency. We can't see this
      information and we don't receive a copy. Money-saved figures in Stats are estimates calculated on your device.
    </p>
    <p>TossLess does not sync between devices. If you delete the app, this information is deleted with it.</p>

    <h3>Barcode lookups (Open Food Facts)</h3>
    <p>
      When you scan a barcode, the app sends only the barcode number to <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org">Open Food Facts</a>, a free public
      food database, to look up the product name, size and category. No other information about you or your list is sent. Like any website, Open
      Food Facts receives your device's IP address when it answers the request. Their
      <a href="https://world.openfoodfacts.org/privacy">privacy policy</a> applies to that. The result is saved on your iPhone so the same product is
      instant next time.
    </p>

    <h3>Camera</h3>
    <p>
      The camera is used only to read barcodes while the scanner is open. No photos or video are saved or sent anywhere. You can turn camera access
      off at any time in iOS Settings › TossLess.
    </p>

    <h3>Reminders</h3>
    <p>
      Daily reminders are local notifications created on your iPhone. They are not sent from a server, and their content, such as “3 things to use
      tonight”, is put together on your device. You can turn them off in the app or in iOS Settings.
    </p>

    <h3>Purchases (TossLess Pro)</h3>
    <p>Payments are handled by Apple through the App Store. We never see your name, Apple ID, email address or payment details.</p>
    <p>
      To know whether your Pro subscription or purchase is active, and to let you restore it, TossLess uses
      <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com">RevenueCat</a>, a service that processes purchases for us. RevenueCat receives:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>A random, anonymous ID created by the app. It is not linked to your name or Apple ID.</li>
      <li>
        Details of your App Store purchases, such as the product, price, currency, dates, trial and renewal status, and the App Store receipt.
      </li>
      <li>Basic technical information, such as app version, iOS version, device type, country or storefront, language and IP address.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      This is used only to provide and check your purchases. It is not used for advertising. See
      <a href="https://www.revenuecat.com/privacy">RevenueCat's privacy policy</a> and
      <a href="https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/">Apple's privacy policy</a>.
    </p>

    <h3>What the app doesn't do</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>No account, sign-up or login.</li>
      <li>No analytics, crash-tracking or advertising tools in the app.</li>
      <li>No tracking across other apps or websites, and no advertising identifier (IDFA).</li>
      <li>No selling or sharing of personal data.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="website">This website</h2>
    <p>This part covers tosslessapp.com, which is separate from the app.</p>

    <h3>Analytics</h3>
    <p>
      We use Cloudflare Web Analytics to count visits and see which pages are read. It does not use cookies and does not track you across sites.
    </p>

    <h3 id="email-signup">Email signup</h3>
    {/* OWNER: review this section, and add your legal basis and retention period if your local law requires them. */}
    <ul>
      <li><strong>What we collect:</strong> the email address you enter in the waitlist form.</li>
      <li><strong>Why:</strong> to email you once when TossLess launches, then occasional food-saving tips.</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Who processes it:</strong> we use Kit (kit.com) to store the list and send the emails. Your address is sent to Kit when you submit the
        form.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Unsubscribing:</strong> every email has an unsubscribe link. You can also write to <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a> and we will
        remove you.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Why we process this information</h2>
    <p>
      Where data protection laws such as the GDPR apply, we process purchase information to provide what you bought (performance of a contract), and
      barcode lookups because you asked for them by scanning (our legitimate interest in providing the feature). We use your email address for the
      waitlist because you asked to join it (consent), and you can withdraw that at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>Keeping and deleting your information</h2>
    <p>
      Information on your iPhone stays until you delete it in the app or delete the app. RevenueCat keeps purchase records for as long as needed to
      provide your purchases and to meet legal and tax obligations. To ask for the purchase data linked to your anonymous ID to be deleted, write to us
      and we'll handle it with RevenueCat. Open Food Facts does not receive anything that identifies you beyond the request itself. Waitlist emails
      are kept until you unsubscribe.
    </p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on where you live, you may have the right to access, correct or delete personal data about you, to object to or limit its use, and to
      complain to your data protection authority. Because almost everything in the app stays on your device, you can see and delete most of it
      yourself there. For anything else, contact us at <a href={mail}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>TossLess is not aimed at children under 13, and we don't knowingly collect personal information from children.</p>

    <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      If we change how TossLess handles information, we'll update this page and the date at the top. Important changes will also be mentioned in the
      app's release notes.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .meta {
    color: var(--text-2);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .summary {
    background: var(--primary-tint);
    border-radius: 14px;
    padding: 1rem;
  }
  h2 {
    padding-top: 1rem;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  h3 {
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0 0.25rem;
  }
</style>
